<section image-layout="blank" id="BblFLMzy0S" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="wLbH1828G7" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">Ozone policy · Investment committee · 23 Sep 2026</p><h1 font-size="46pt">Map the machinery before you price the risk</h1><p font-size="lg">Proposed diligence thesis: exposure sits in substance-dependent equipment and lifecycle obligations—not in broad sector labels. Separate legacy ozone-depleting substances from HFC climate exposure; validate the asset inventory; then price timing, capex and operating resilience.</p><spacer size="20pt"></spacer><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Screening perimeter:</b> refrigeration · HVAC · foam · fire suppression · industrial processes</p></grid-item><grid-item id="YjKjeNyR-t" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/wHnkhVXJiuFksl97P2xAz.png" saved-media-id="cupvvlggk7n080u" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="industrial-atmospheric-relief" alt="Precision editorial relief construction of atmospheric layers intersecting with a refrigeration compressor, cooling coil, recovery cylinder and valves, built from matte mineral paper and oxidized metal under cool raking studio light, exposure blue, transition teal, restrained rust accents and charcoal shadows, no text, no lettering, no logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="frvsxtIFzF" background-color="heading" padding="12pt 16pt"><p font-size="14pt">Conceptual equipment relief · cooling compressor, coil, cylinder and valves · not portfolio assets</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="eSTVyqpTmT"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="GnrWcibA7l" padding="42pt 48pt 24pt" colspan="45"><h2>Underwriting starts with classification</h2><p>UNEP’s 2023 assessment projects return to 1980 ozone levels <b>if current policies remain in place</b>.</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="DfNs6bJx4H" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><p font-size="30pt"><b>2040</b> <span font-size="14pt">Global</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="aEH1bbMg11" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><p font-size="30pt"><b>2045</b> <span font-size="14pt">Arctic</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="HqcRfsupIg" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><p font-size="30pt"><b>2066</b> <span font-size="14pt">Antarctica</span></p></grid-item></grid><table col-widths="[14,34,52]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 4pt 7pt; font-size: 15pt; line-height: 1.25;"><tbody><tr><td><p>Class</p></td><td><p>Science and policy</p></td><td><p>Investment read-through</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>ODS</b></p></td><td><p>Depletes ozone; Montreal Protocol phaseout.</p></td><td><p>Test installed base, servicing, recovery and disposal.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>HFC</b></p></td><td><p>Warms climate; does not deplete ozone. Kigali is related but distinct.</p></td><td><p>Test replacement timing, supply, capex and resilience.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Unknown</b></p></td><td><p>No reliable classification yet.</p></td><td><p>Verify substance, use and jurisdiction before pricing.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p font-size="13pt"><b>Legal boundary:</b> the supplied sources establish global treaty architecture, not current jurisdiction-specific compliance dates. <b>Sources:</b> <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP 2023 assessment summary</a>; <a href="https://ozone.unep.org/treaties/montreal-protocol">Montreal Protocol</a>.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="dGMReiSQ9I" padding="0" colspan="15"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/gADT1E7M2xArfmm0FEgym.png" saved-media-id="hrz3589y8ki6rl2" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="industrial-atmospheric-relief" alt="Precision editorial relief cross-section of layered stratosphere above an abstract refrigeration system, a compressor and coiled tubing connected beneath translucent mineral-paper atmospheric bands, oxidized metal details, cool raking light, exposure blue and transition teal with one restrained rust signal, no text, no lettering, no logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="VlAQY5vsx0" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="5Sl7IEHByP"><h2>Map equipment and substances before mapping sectors</h2><p>For each holding, establish five coordinates before concluding on exposure.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="8tHC9PgT6x" colspan="12"><h4>Substance</h4><p>ODS, HFC, lower-impact substitute, or unknown.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="SV8selxd90" colspan="12"><h4>Asset</h4><p>Refrigeration, HVAC, foam, fire suppression, or industrial process.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="G2W5GljSTR" colspan="12"><h4>Lifecycle</h4><p>Installation, servicing, replacement, recovery, or disposal.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="J7AlM0nf-E" colspan="12"><h4>Value channel</h4><p>Capex, operating cost, downtime, compliance, or customer access.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="lW3pQhaoBY" colspan="12"><h4>Action</h4><p>Underwrite, reserve, engage, monitor, or defer.</p></grid-item></grid><aside><p><b>Investment implication:</b> a sector label cannot substitute for equipment and substance evidence.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="WDsoujL6-S" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="r_89BvvHDG"><h2>Policy reaches value through physical systems</h2><p>Move from policy to valuation only through a validated transmission chain.</p><grid marker="number" marker-size="large" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="chevron" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-fill="true" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="1em" style="--marker-chip-padding: 0.75em;"><grid-item id="0KM0NVXwt-" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Substance + asset</p><h4>Policy scope</h4><p>Identify the relevant substance, use and jurisdiction.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="R6ANQnK9U6" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Lifecycle</p><h4>Operational constraint</h4><p>Test equipment, servicing, supply and end-of-life handling.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="nO4yM6OwjB" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Value channel</p><h4>Financial transmission</h4><p>Test capex, maintenance, downtime, working capital and margins.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="3ge3ABMSp1" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Action</p><h4>Valuation response</h4><p>Adjust only when exposure and timing are evidenced.</p></grid-item></grid><aside variant="warning"><p>Unknown substance inventories reduce underwriting confidence before they prove financial loss.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="VtBnZfD_1x"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="V1SnVOAtTh"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative example · Not portfolio data</p><h2>Exposure matrix: transition urgency × financial materiality</h2><freeform-block w="840" h="320"><box type="content" x="80" y="20" w="370" h="125" sizing="fixed" locked="true" background-color="rgba(45,111,142,0.07)"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="450" y="20" w="370" h="125" sizing="fixed" locked="true" background-color="rgba(182,78,60,0.10)"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="80" y="145" w="370" h="125" sizing="fixed" locked="true" background-color="rgba(93,102,107,0.05)"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="450" y="145" w="370" h="125" sizing="fixed" locked="true" background-color="rgba(40,122,114,0.07)"><p></p></box><shape preset="line" x="80" y="270" w="740" h="2" locked="true" stroke="neutral-border" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="80" y="20" w="2" h="250" locked="true" stroke="neutral-border" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="450" y="20" w="2" h="250" locked="true" stroke="neutral-border" stroke-width="1"></shape><shape preset="line" x="80" y="145" w="740" h="2" locked="true" stroke="neutral-border" stroke-width="1"></shape><box type="content" y="22" w="70"><p font-size="14pt" align="right"><b>HIGH</b><br>materiality</p></box><box type="content" x="10" y="240" w="60"><p font-size="14pt" align="right"><b>LOW</b></p></box><box type="content" x="82" y="282" w="210"><p font-size="14pt">LOW transition urgency</p></box><box type="content" x="610" y="282" w="210"><p font-size="14pt" align="right">HIGH transition urgency</p></box><box type="content" x="94" y="24" w="180"><p font-size="14pt"><b>PLAN / RESERVE</b></p></box><box type="content" x="464" y="24" w="170"><p font-size="14pt"><b>ACT NOW</b></p></box><box type="content" x="94" y="149" w="150"><p font-size="14pt"><b>MONITOR</b></p></box><box type="content" x="464" y="149" w="220"><p font-size="14pt"><b>VERIFY / DEFER IF MATERIAL</b></p></box><box type="content" x="190" y="48" w="240" h="88" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-3" style="padding: 8pt 10pt;"><h4 font-size="16pt">PLAN · HFC</h4><p font-size="16pt">HFC-heavy supermarket estate<br>U3 · M4 · Plan capex</p></box><box type="content" x="570" y="48" w="235" h="88" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-2" style="padding: 8pt 10pt;"><h4 font-size="16pt">ACT NOW · ODS</h4><p font-size="16pt">Legacy-ODS cold store<br>U4 · M4 · <b>Reserve + engage</b></p></box><box type="content" x="130" y="174" w="260" h="82" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 8pt 10pt;"><h4 font-size="16pt">MONITOR · INDIRECT</h4><p font-size="16pt">Landlord-controlled HVAC<br>U1 · M1 · Monitor</p></box><box type="content" x="535" y="174" w="255" h="82" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-1" style="padding: 8pt 10pt;"><h4 font-size="16pt">VERIFY · UNKNOWN</h4><p font-size="16pt">Older fire suppression<br>U3 · M2 · Defer if material</p></box></freeform-block><p font-size="16pt"><b>Illustrative holdings and scores:</b> U = urgency; M = materiality; 5 = highest. Confirm all five coordinates before action.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="APEXmRzCFA" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="S58uhxmeyA"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative assumptions · Not forecasts</p><h2>Stress the transition, not the recovery forecast</h2><p>Apply these sensitivities only after validating the equipment and substance inventory.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="wZVRIv60GP" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="outline">Base</label></labels><h3>Planned replacement</h3><ul><li>Planned replacement cycle</li><li>Servicing cost +5%</li><li>No incremental downtime</li></ul></grid-item><grid-item id="RhRESiRTjy" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="solid">Tighter transition</label></labels><h3>Earlier capex</h3><ul><li>Replacement three years earlier</li><li>Capex +12%</li><li>Transition-year EBITDA margin −1 percentage point</li></ul></grid-item><grid-item id="cT1m56oiqs" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="solid">Supply disruption</label></labels><h3>Capacity pressure</h3><ul><li>Equipment lead time +6 months</li><li>Servicing cost +20%</li><li>Temporary capacity constraint</li></ul></grid-item></grid><aside><p>Revalue with issuer-specific timing, contracts and financing capacity.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="5eNqILnn-0" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="6XcDyb3DBT"><h2>Minimum evidence for an investable transition plan</h2><p>Run all four checks; then use evidence completeness and potential materiality to set the gate.</p><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="P4ijkQsSmf" colspan="36"><h3>Minimum evidence pack</h3><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="rounded" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="wgB2vofDtQ" padding="8pt 0"><p>Inventory by substance, equipment, location, age and ownership.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="JVC6ukYf6M" padding="8pt 0"><p>Leak, maintenance, servicing, recovery and disposal records.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="wmAecjJt2i" padding="8pt 0"><p>Replacement schedule, approved capex, suppliers and technician capacity.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Q7enDgMmgD" padding="8pt 0"><p>Scenario ownership and board-level accountability.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="Lryg7gN9ea" colspan="24"><h3>Evidence-to-action gate</h3><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="ntMtt8OYtb" background-color="palette-3" padding="13pt 16pt"><h4>Underwrite</h4><p>All four checks reconcile and the response is funded.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="MwqmF4eVQM" background-color="palette-1" padding="13pt 16pt"><h4>Reserve + engage</h4><p>Gaps are bounded, priceable and assigned to a named owner.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="QPfe3gVk_5" background-color="palette-2" padding="13pt 16pt"><h4>Defer</h4><p>A potentially material exposure remains unclassified or unfunded.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ijzyGjGFnA" vertical-align="center" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="qtRpEHi_lu"><p role="eyebrow">Committee decision</p><h1 font-size="38pt">Turn unknowns into priced evidence</h1><h3 role="subheading">Approve a 90-day portfolio screen with one investment-committee gate.</h3><grid marker="number" marker-size="large" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-straddle="true" spacing="medium" padding-top="28pt"><grid-item id="lMChLylpDx" background-color="surface" text-color="#171A1F" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Days 0–30</p><h4>Prioritize assets</h4><p font-size="18pt">Screen refrigeration, cooling, foam, fire suppression and process dependence.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="IBibzDdmbX" background-color="surface" text-color="#171A1F" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Days 31–60</p><h4>Classify substances</h4><p font-size="18pt">Assign ODS, HFC, lower-impact substitute or unknown; request missing inventories.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="YItiKsKlfe" background-color="surface" text-color="#171A1F" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Days 61–90</p><h4>Price the cases</h4><p font-size="18pt">Apply issuer timing, contracts and financing capacity to the illustrative stresses.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="gadtcSHIpc" background-color="surface" text-color="#171A1F" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">IC gate</p><h4>Choose the action</h4><p font-size="18pt">Underwrite, reserve + engage or defer; set the owner and reporting cadence.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer size="12pt"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="tUjVXhilJU" background-color="palette-2" padding="12pt 16pt"><h3>No substance map, no confident transition valuation.</h3></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>